The two-pass structure maps directly to Erik's document — I kept his
for-loops verbatim and only added framing, "choosing iteration
points", and the Pitfalls section.

The skill intentionally doesn't bundle a script for finding iteration
points; that felt like premature automation for a first version.

The description is deliberately long — it needs to hit several distinct
trigger phrases ("far behind", "stale branch", "too many conflicts",
"iteratively") that are semantically related but don't share a single
keyword, so the length is load-bearing.

One uncertainty: `tac` in Step 2 is standard on Linux but requires
coreutils or a `tail -r` substitute on macOS. Left as-is from Erik's
original document.
